        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A market premium is an economic instrument that ensures a guaranteed remuneration, e.g. a fixed feed-in tariff, by paying to the producing agent the difference between a guaranteed return on a good/product and the monetary price for which the good/product is traded on the market.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="de">Marktprämie</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">market premium</rdfs:label>
        <oeo:OEO_00020426>issue: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/issues/839
